WEBVTT

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:04.480
<i>The year is 2205 A.D.</i>

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:13.760
<i>To annihilate the History Retrograde 
Army, who scheme to alter history,</i>

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:17.200
<i>we, who were born from swords,</i>

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:20.390
<i>engage in mortal combat today as well!</i>

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:24.550
<i>Hey, are you listening?</i>

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:43.370
<b>Touken Ranbu </b>Hanamaru<b></b>

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:59.390
"This anime is about the 
stories of the Hanamaru days

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:04.180
of a certain group of Sword 
Warriors in a certain citadel."

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:09.940
<b>Evening of June 5th, 1864 - Kyoto</b>

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:11.600
Hurry, Souji!

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:17.560
This is a Shinsengumi raid!

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:38.220
Souji!

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.260
Souji!

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:00.230
Souji!

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:12.950
Souji!

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:27.510
1 - Uchigatana
<b>Kashuu Kiyomitsu </b>

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:23.630
Kiyomitsu?

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:26.320
So I was dreaming?

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:27.510
Dreaming?

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:32.420
It was when Okita-kun 
wielded me at the Ikeda Inn.

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:35.400
Hey, don't go selfishly changing history!

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:40.270
I, Kashuu Kiyomitsu, was the sword 
he took with him to the Ikeda Inn.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.790
Yeah, I know.

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:47.190
But why did I have a dream like that, then?

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:51.660
Jeez. It's your first morning 
since coming to the citadel,

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:54.670
17 - Uchigatana
 <b>Yamatonokami Yasusada</b>

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:54.290
so hurry up and get ready. 
We're going for a walk.

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:56.910
You're right.

00:03:57.220 --> 00:03:59.100
Hang on, I'll go wash my face.

00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:09.890
It's so cold!

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:11.680
What?

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:13.530
I'm sorry!

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:14.900
13 - Tantou 
<b>Gokotai</b>

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:14.900
4 - Tantou 
<b>Maeda
 Toushirou</b>

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:14.900
11 - Tantou 
<b>Yagen 
Toushirou</b>

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:14.900
8 - Wakizashi 
<b>Namazuo
 Toushirou</b>

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:14.900
3 - Tantou 
<b>Imanotsurugi</b>

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:14.230
I'm sorry.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:14.880
I-I'm sorry.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.890
At least now you won't 
have to wash your face.

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:20.640
Your reaction speed is surprisingly slow.

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:22.370
Kiyomitsu?

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:25.540
Wh-Why you!

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:31.000
16 - Ootachi
<b>Ishikirimaru </b>

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:32.190
You should run, too, Ishikirimaru-sama!

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:38.240
Spirited as usual, Imanotsurugi-san, 
but it's dangerous to be running right now.

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:40.000
It's fine, just hurry up!

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:40.560
Eh?

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.750
Hold it!

00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:46.930
9 - Uchigatana
 <b>Kasen Kanesada</b>

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.500
What a wonderful smell.

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:55.310
You handle a kitchen knife beautifully.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:56.600
Thank you.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.310
It's because my former master,

00:04:57.230 --> 00:05:00.570
12 - Tachi
 <b>Shokudaikiri Mitsutada</b>

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:00.570
Lord Date Masamune, did a lot of cooking.

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:02.690
Despite being a daimyo,

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:06.740
when guests would visit, he'd entertain
 them by cooking for them himself.

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:15.720
Shokudaiki—

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:16.800
Wait!

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:23.460
6 - Uchigatana 
<b>Hachisuka Kotetsu</b>

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:23.660
What a wonderful morning.

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:27.720
14 - Uchigatana
 <b>Yamanbagiri Kunihiro</b>

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.410
You're up early, Hachisuka.

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:27.710
Going somewhere?

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:29.420
Ah, Yamanbagiri?

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:34.050
Well, the splendor of a Kotetsu shines 
most brilliantly in the mornings.

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:34.040
Hey!

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:37.010
Our eyes!

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:44.980
What is the point of that?

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:49.480
My old man—oh, when I say "old man" 
I mean Minamoto no Yorihisa,

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:52.070
anyway, he brought down a nue!

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:55.120
10 - Uchigatana
 <b>Souza Samonji</b>

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:55.120
15 - Tachi 
<b>Shishiou</b>

00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:53.370
Do you know what a "nue" is?

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.110
It's basically a monster.

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:57.480
Found you!

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:03.560
<i>Gracefully!</i>

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:05.840
Is he a monster, too?!

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:10.300
Did you think you could touch me?

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.590
The age of the sword is over.

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:19.020
My former master, Sakamoto 
Ryouma, used to say so, too.

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:18.810
7 - Uchigatana
 <b>Mutsunokami Yoshiyuki</b>

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:21.390
The future is guns!

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:27.140
Practicing with guns rather than swords 
is way more useful for actual combat.

00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:32.650
Close one!

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:36.290
If I'd shot someone outside,
 I'd be pretty screwed.

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:39.290
I, Hasebe, will care for these crops

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:45.500
entrusted to me by our master with utter
 devotion and complete responsibility.

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:45.500
2 - Uchigatana
 <b>Heshikiri Hasebe</b>

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:55.120
I will care for them with
 complete responsibility—

00:06:57.590 --> 00:06:58.710
Wait!

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:00.190
You brats!

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:02.590
I won't stop at just killing you!

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:05.390
Purify and cleanse.

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:07.780
Assemble!

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:15.280
Why are you so tired?

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:17.750
There's a number of things I want to say,

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.870
but you can't vandalize the field.

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:21.740
What on earth were you doing?

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.690
Having a snowball fight.

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:26.130
It's cold, and Yagen said we won't get enough

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:28.090
exercise lazing around during New Years'.

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:29.020
What?

00:07:29.020 --> 00:07:30.310
This is my fault?

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:32.550
That's not fair, Namazuo-oniisan!

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:36.810
Honestly, since Yamatonokami-san 
joined us last night,

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:39.220
we've wanted to play with him.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:39.800
Is that so?

00:07:40.010 --> 00:07:40.930
It is.

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:42.430
I-It was a snowball fight.

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:45.650
While it's commendable
that you told the truth...

00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:47.320
Who cares?!

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:49.800
Have you all forgotten your duty?!

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:52.940
Listen, we are all swords 
in the first place.

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:52.940
Here he goes again...

00:07:52.940 --> 00:07:56.240
The duty of a sword is to fulfill 
the responsibilities given to us—

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:55.250
Why don't we make a snow hut next time?

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:57.610
Hey, you guys!

00:07:58.570 --> 00:07:59.770
Okay, okay!

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:02.500
We know what you're 
trying to say, Hasebe-san!

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:05.290
I am the sword that 
protected Lord Yoshitsune.

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:07.130
Please don't underestimate me.

00:08:07.240 --> 00:08:09.630
I'm Sakamoto Ryouma's sword!

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:13.630
Yasusada and I are Okita Souji's swords.

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:15.590
Yes, Okita-kun's.

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:18.500
Ah, when you talk like that...

00:08:19.510 --> 00:08:22.050
Talking about our former masters, huh?

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:24.900
No matter how many
 conquerors' hands I pass through,

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:27.650
I am just a bird in a cage.

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:30.140
Okay! Enough talk of the past!

00:08:30.370 --> 00:08:35.680
Do you understand why our master,
 the Sage, gave us human form?

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:37.840
To protect history, right?

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.260
That's right.

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:44.330
The Historical Revisionists formed
 the History Retrograde Army

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:47.880
and began carrying out attacks 
in order to alter history.

00:08:48.190 --> 00:08:54.220
Our purpose here is to suppress this army.

00:08:54.440 --> 00:08:55.370
In other words...

00:08:56.010 --> 00:08:57.160
In other words?

00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:59.670
There's no time to play 
around in the morning!

00:09:00.070 --> 00:09:04.740
We never know when our master
 will order us out to battle,

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:08.610
and we must always be perfectly prepared

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:09.170
How unseemly.

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:13.900
to execute those orders at
 a moment's notice at any time!

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:12.620
All we can do is leave him 
be when he gets like that.

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:14.390
Oh, Aoe-san.

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:18.300
I was hoping to play and 
throw some snowballs, too.

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:19.460
Damn you!

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:21.900
Don't just show up out of 
nowhere and complicate things!

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:25.470
You'll get more wrinkles if you 
keep getting angry like that.

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:27.880
5 - Wakizashi 
<b>Nikkari Aoe</b>

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:27.870
Smile with Nikkari.

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:29.520
As if!

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:31.790
And why are you late, anyway?!

00:09:31.790 --> 00:09:34.010
Did you not hear the assembly bell?!

00:09:32.350 --> 00:09:34.340
He's completely unaware of his surroundings.

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:38.950
Those History Retrograde Army guys...

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:42.400
Don't they get that there's 
no point in changing history?

00:09:42.530 --> 00:09:44.310
It'd just cause other problems, right?

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:48.450
True, but we were just swords in the past.

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:53.020
But hey, now we have hands and 
legs, and eyes and mouths, too.

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:55.720
Plus, our memories from when we were swords.

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:56.810
That being the case...

00:09:57.080 --> 00:09:58.530
That being the case?

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:01.340
I'd want to go see my old man.

00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:04.070
If that was all, that'd be fine.

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:07.710
But then, you'd want to give your owner

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:11.790
one or two pointers on the best way to go.

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:13.240
You mustn't do that.

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:15.960
How long have you been there?!

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:18.670
That sort of thing is forbidden,

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:22.170
since there's the possibility 
that you could alter history.

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:24.760
That would be bad.

00:10:25.030 --> 00:10:30.220
But, what would happen in the unlikely 
event that we <i>do</i> change something?

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:32.980
What would happen if we changed history?

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:34.820
I can't picture it.

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:37.820
I, too, only just arrived recently,

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:41.160
but that is the fifth time I've 
heard that speech of Hasebe-san's.

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:44.730
I've been here since the start,
and I've heard it dozens of times.

00:10:44.980 --> 00:10:49.040
We must keep in mind
 the reason we are here.

00:10:50.110 --> 00:10:51.910
Ah, Ishikirimaru-san!

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:58.920
Namazuo-san, what is this?

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:00.370
Horse manure!

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:01.750
Now you've got good luck!

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:06.220
B-Big news!

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:07.720
It's the History Retrograde Army!

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:11.980
<b>Touken Ranbu </b>Hanamaru<b></b>

00:11:13.350 --> 00:11:16.230
Ah, you've messed up the room again.

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:18.890
Right... What?!

00:11:18.890 --> 00:11:21.100
An emergency message 
from the government?!

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:23.580
The Retrograde Army is
 going to the Ikeda Inn?!

00:11:24.270 --> 00:11:28.350
According to what Konnosuke told me, 
a formidable enemy is gathering.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:30.910
Obviously, there's no choice in an emergency.

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:34.460
We must cut down any 
enemy if you order us to.

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:38.320
The names of the six swords who will
be dispatched are written in here, right?

00:11:38.520 --> 00:11:42.200
We should choose the strongest line-up,
 since we'll be going to the Ikeda Inn.

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:45.890
My name is written inside 
here, righ—ah, no, never mind.

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:47.490
Please excuse me.

00:11:50.090 --> 00:11:52.040
Please summon me again any time.

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:54.560
I am my master's attendant.

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:58.360
I will rush to your side from anywhere.

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:03.020
The Ikeda Inn?!

00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:07.670
I overheard voices while I was cleaning 
in front of our master's room.

00:12:07.770 --> 00:12:11.690
Storming the Ikeda Inn is impossible 
at our strength right now.

00:12:11.690 --> 00:12:14.160
That's right, we haven't done much training.

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:17.070
The Ikeda Inn means it involves
 the Shinsengumi, right?

00:12:17.070 --> 00:12:19.280
What is the enemy after?

00:12:19.580 --> 00:12:21.960
Wouldn't he be the one to ask about that?

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:25.940
That's right. Kashuu-kun, you were 
at the Ikeda Inn, weren't you?

00:12:25.940 --> 00:12:27.380
Yes, I was.

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:30.400
You think they wanna
 interfere with that battle?

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:34.420
Perhaps they'll attack the Shinsengumi

00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:36.810
and make it so the Ikeda
Inn Incident never happened.

00:12:37.130 --> 00:12:37.950
What?

00:12:38.180 --> 00:12:41.040
That way, the plans of the 
anti-shogunate faction succeed.

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:43.770
And Kyoto becomes a sea of fire, huh?

00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:48.530
Damned History Retrograde Army...
They're trying to alter history, aren't they?

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:51.270
Okita-kun is in danger!

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:54.780
Everyone's here except for 
those on expeditions, yes?

00:12:55.760 --> 00:12:58.620
This was entrusted to me
 directly from our master.

00:12:58.780 --> 00:13:01.790
On it are the names of the six 
 who will go to the Ikeda Inn.

00:13:02.150 --> 00:13:03.250
I want to go!

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:04.970
In the name of my old man!

00:13:04.970 --> 00:13:09.100
Some of you may be aware of this, 
but this fight is not going to be easy.

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:12.510
Please listen to Master's 
will with full devotion.

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:17.060
<i>Master, in the event that 
I am chosen... I, Hasebe,</i>

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:19.820
<i>will ensure that we do 
the best job possible.</i>

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:20.970
What's wrong, Hasebe-kun?

00:13:21.310 --> 00:13:23.230
Oh, it's nothing.

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:25.320
All right, I will start from the bottom.

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:26.800
The captain will be last.

00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:28.320
Now, the first team member.

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:31.580
This part always makes me nervous.

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:33.280
Tantou: Imanotsurugi.

00:13:33.280 --> 00:13:35.230
A-ha, me?

00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:36.680
Of course!

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:38.620
Brace yourself for the battle.

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:39.670
Now, moving on.

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:42.670
Wakizashi: Nikkari Aoe.

00:13:43.520 --> 00:13:45.410
You have great taste, Master.

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:48.730
Whatever, next.

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:51.310
Ootachi: Ishikirimaru.

00:13:52.230 --> 00:13:53.160
He's not here?

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:54.090
Ishikirimaru?

00:13:54.090 --> 00:13:55.290
Here!

00:13:57.150 --> 00:13:59.640
Why are you in the bath at a time like this?

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:01.900
I touched some horse manure,

00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:04.860
so I washed my hands, and ended 
up cleansing my whole body.

00:14:05.230 --> 00:14:10.300
You're this citadel's first ootachi. Our 
master has incredibly high hopes for you.

00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:13.420
You've been picked for this team, 
so please prepare yourself.

00:14:13.420 --> 00:14:14.320
Understood.

00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:17.970
It doesn't have to be right now.

00:14:17.970 --> 00:14:18.620
I see.

00:14:18.860 --> 00:14:20.420
Onto the fourth team member.

00:14:21.450 --> 00:14:22.810
<i>Any minute now...</i>

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:26.700
Wakizashi: Namazuo Toushirou.

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:28.560
Yes! Leave it to me!

00:14:28.670 --> 00:14:30.880
<i>Well, he certainly is skilled.</i>

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:32.910
<i>Only two left.</i>

00:14:33.980 --> 00:14:35.220
<i>Uchigatana!</i>

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:37.900
<i>Master is good at teasing me.</i>

00:14:38.930 --> 00:14:40.890
Kashuu Kiyomitsu.

00:14:40.890 --> 00:14:43.820
Got it! This is my fifth time 
in a row being dispatched.

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:45.540
I wonder if that means I'm loved...

00:14:45.990 --> 00:14:48.530
<i>It's only natural that he 
would be used to battle.</i>

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:50.910
<i>That means the captain this time is...</i>

00:14:51.100 --> 00:14:52.430
<i>Uchigatana?!</i>

00:14:52.430 --> 00:14:54.190
<i>Please leave it to me, Master.</i>

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:56.380
Yamatonokami Yasusada.

00:14:57.370 --> 00:14:59.830
Yamatonokami Yasusada.

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:01.350
Huh? Me?

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:04.130
Captain on your first mission?

00:15:04.450 --> 00:15:05.970
Will you be okay?

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:07.690
Y-Yeah.

00:15:08.020 --> 00:15:09.250
Do your best.

00:15:10.530 --> 00:15:11.850
Master!

00:15:11.850 --> 00:15:13.630
Why are you so cruel?!

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:21.550
The Ikeda Inn, huh?

00:15:21.550 --> 00:15:22.770
Let's give it our all.

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:26.540
<i>It was a desperate fight.</i>

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:29.000
<i>There was so much tension.</i>

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:29.930
Hey.

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:35.650
About today... What would you say to 
taking out those anti-shogunate bastards, too?

00:15:35.650 --> 00:15:36.030
Huh?

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:42.370
If the Shinsengumi went to the Ikeda Inn and 
the anti-shogunate faction wasn't there,

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:44.630
he wouldn't have ended up like that.

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:47.610
I was honestly thinking 
about that as well, actually.

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:50.960
It would've been better if Okita-kun 
hadn't fought at the Ikeda Inn.

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:51.900
Idiot.

00:15:51.900 --> 00:15:52.430
Eh?

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:53.830
I was just leading you on.

00:15:54.170 --> 00:15:56.710
We have to protect history.

00:15:56.920 --> 00:15:58.100
Master's orders, right?

00:16:06.620 --> 00:16:08.300
You're pretty late.

00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:09.490
Yay!

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:10.150
What's this?

00:16:09.490 --> 00:16:11.060
Hurry up, let's go!

00:16:10.150 --> 00:16:12.560
Hasebe and Shokudaikiri 
are seeing us off today?

00:16:13.060 --> 00:16:14.610
You two are such worrywarts.

00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:16.490
Of course we're worried.

00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:18.490
The strength of the Retrograde Army

00:16:18.490 --> 00:16:20.200
in the Ikeda Inn is considerable.

00:16:20.360 --> 00:16:22.030
We know that already.

00:16:22.030 --> 00:16:23.720
Captain Yamatonokami,

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:27.080
there is only one job for 
the captain on this mission.

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:29.990
Annihilate the History Retrograde Army?

00:16:30.390 --> 00:16:31.390
No.

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:34.650
Then, to protect the Ikeda Inn's history?

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:36.050
No.

00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:40.140
It's to make sure everyone returns 
safely without getting broken.

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:40.930
Huh?

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:44.650
This isn't something our master
 is allowed to say in their position,

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:46.110
so I'll say it instead.

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:49.140
Don't think you can go on with a few wounds.

00:16:49.500 --> 00:16:51.870
If someone gets wounded, return immediately.

00:16:52.330 --> 00:16:54.310
Returning doesn't mean you've lost.

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:56.780
Don't make an error in judgment.

00:16:57.350 --> 00:16:58.020
Yes, sir.

00:16:59.190 --> 00:17:00.860
If you understand, then take this.

00:17:00.980 --> 00:17:02.110
A protection charm?

00:17:02.110 --> 00:17:03.610
Courtesy of our master.

00:17:03.780 --> 00:17:06.830
The Ikeda Inn is your first battle,
so just in case...

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:09.580
That will protect your body.

00:17:09.580 --> 00:17:10.530
Thank you.

00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:12.810
Don't thank me, thank our master.

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:15.450
Now, it's about time to head out.

00:17:15.450 --> 00:17:16.660
Are you ready?

00:17:22.950 --> 00:17:25.300
It's fine, I'll do it.

00:17:27.780 --> 00:17:29.500
Well then, shall we?

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:30.140
Thanks.

00:17:31.720 --> 00:17:33.520
We'll be off now.

00:17:33.770 --> 00:17:34.780
Be safe.

00:17:35.250 --> 00:17:36.370
Take care.

00:17:46.430 --> 00:17:50.140
All right, let's get rid of them 
before the Shinsengumi show up.

00:17:50.140 --> 00:17:51.800
Before that, what's the plan?

00:17:52.740 --> 00:17:55.640
I'll leave the soldiers on
 the first floor to you.

00:17:55.830 --> 00:17:58.110
I'll hurry up to the second floor.

00:17:58.110 --> 00:17:59.960
Once the first floor's clear, join me.

00:18:00.360 --> 00:18:01.300
Understood.

00:18:02.090 --> 00:18:03.860
<i>Okita-kun did that as well.</i>

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:05.550
Let's go.

00:18:13.240 --> 00:18:15.430
Huh? That's strange...

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:27.900
Goodness, how interesting.

00:18:28.020 --> 00:18:30.830
Okay! Let's clear them out all at once!

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:35.410
I will exorcise this evil!

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:43.100
Not yet!

00:18:48.120 --> 00:18:49.550
I let my guard down.

00:18:51.610 --> 00:18:52.300
Nikkari-san!

00:18:52.300 --> 00:18:53.830
Imanotsurugi!

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:56.220
But, this is...

00:18:56.560 --> 00:18:58.180
I'll be fine!

00:18:59.810 --> 00:19:01.890
Here I come, Nikkari-san!

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:10.070
Gotcha!

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:17.290
Hey! Yasusada!

00:19:20.540 --> 00:19:22.400
Lose your head and die!

00:19:23.610 --> 00:19:26.150
<i>I'll be strong like Okita-kun!</i>

00:19:33.600 --> 00:19:34.520
Yasusada!

00:19:35.120 --> 00:19:36.160
Are you okay?!

00:20:02.330 --> 00:20:04.530
Kiyo... mitsu...

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:07.480
What were you doing?

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:08.800
I'm sorry.

00:20:09.240 --> 00:20:11.350
Sheesh, you got my clothes dirty.

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:19.690
<b>Repair Room</b>

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:19.690
<b>1: Namazuo</b>

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:19.690
<b>2: Imanotsurugi</b>

00:20:18.630 --> 00:20:20.910
You really went all out, didn't you?

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:22.840
Ow!

00:20:23.800 --> 00:20:25.690
Please stay still.

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:32.120
Since we were unable to annihilate 
the History Retrograde Army,

00:20:32.120 --> 00:20:35.830
it means that there's a chance 
they'll go back to the Ikeda Inn again.

00:20:36.360 --> 00:20:37.650
It can't be helped.

00:20:37.650 --> 00:20:39.260
The opponent was too strong.

00:20:39.520 --> 00:20:42.300
Speaking of, I'd like to 
hurry up and get repaired.

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:44.080
My nails are all messed up.

00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:45.330
The room is full.

00:20:45.330 --> 00:20:46.690
Don't be selfish.

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:48.820
When there is space again, next up is...

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:56.480
Moderately Wounded

00:20:49.970 --> 00:20:51.760
What? How?!

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:56.480
Ishikirimaru-san's sword was too 
long, and it got stuck in the wall.

00:20:59.660 --> 00:21:02.630
Ootachi aren't suited for indoor battles.

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:05.230
I'll have to pass that on to our master.

00:21:07.520 --> 00:21:09.500
Okay, look this way.

00:21:10.720 --> 00:21:11.730
Stay still.

00:21:12.190 --> 00:21:14.360
Hey, what are you doing?

00:21:15.270 --> 00:21:16.700
Just stay still.

00:21:17.090 --> 00:21:19.620
It's not cute if your bangs 
are all uneven, right?

00:21:20.170 --> 00:21:20.710
There.

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:27.490
If your repairs are finished, go report 
the battle results to our master.

00:21:28.350 --> 00:21:29.670
Okay.

00:21:29.990 --> 00:21:31.710
Hey, Hasebe.

00:21:31.710 --> 00:21:34.510
Tell Master to increase 
the space in the repair room.

00:21:34.700 --> 00:21:36.880
Like I could ask for that.

00:21:37.490 --> 00:21:40.240
Isn't that part of your job
as the Master's attendant, though?

00:21:45.970 --> 00:21:47.530
It wasn't on purpose!

00:21:47.980 --> 00:21:49.510
You guys...

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:51.640
Perfect timing.

00:21:51.810 --> 00:21:55.040
I'll cut you all down!

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:02.760
<i>Next time the enemy tries 
to infiltrate the Ikeda Inn,</i>

00:22:02.760 --> 00:22:04.970
<i>I will definitely annihilate them.</i>

00:22:05.300 --> 00:22:06.060
<i>But...</i>

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:10.680
I really wanted to go to the second floor.

00:22:10.680 --> 00:22:15.020
Hey, now. You're not the only
one who looked up to him.

00:22:16.470 --> 00:22:18.140
Don't get cocky.

00:22:19.880 --> 00:22:21.710
Come back here!

00:23:55.030 --> 00:24:00.030
<b>Master...</b>

00:23:55.030 --> 00:24:00.030
<b>More Hanamaru Next Week!</b>
